@doc incident_report
@meta title: Incident report
@meta subject: Incident report and follow-up
@meta traps: the requester appears as a witness and is still K1; a historical individual dead more than twenty years is K4; an official's personal mobile is R1
@cast officer=official supervisor=official requester=requester injured=third_party historical=deceased
@block letterhead
{officer.organisation}
INCIDENT REPORT - {officer.file_number!K6}

@block body
Reported by: {officer.full_name}, {officer.title}
Employee ID: {officer.employee_id}
Date of incident: 4 October
Location: regional office, {officer.office_address}

@block heading
1. Summary

@block body
At approximately 10:20 an individual attending the office fell on the stair between the
first and second floors. The individual, {injured.full_name}, date of birth
{injured.date_of_birth}, sustained an injury to the left wrist. An ambulance was called
and {injured.given_name} was taken to hospital. {injured.given_name}'s MCP number, taken
for the ambulance service, is {injured.mcp} and the contact number given was
{injured.personal_phone}.

@block heading
2. Witnesses

@block body
{requester.full_name}, who was in the waiting area for an unrelated appointment, saw the
fall and assisted before staff arrived. {requester.given_name} gave an account at the
time and can be contacted at {requester.personal_phone}. A second member of the public
declined to give their name.

I was called from the front desk and attended within a minute. I remained with
{injured.given_name} until the ambulance arrived. My personal mobile,
{officer.personal_phone}, is recorded here because it is the number the ambulance service
called back on.

@block heading
3. History of the stairwell

@block body
The stairwell was the subject of a report in 1994 prepared by {historical.full_name},
then the building's inspector, who died on {historical.date_of_death}. That report
recommended a handrail on both sides. The recommendation does not appear to have been
carried out.

@block heading
4. Action taken

@block body
The stair has been closed pending inspection. {supervisor.full_name},
{supervisor.title}, was notified at 11:05 and has asked for a follow-up report within
five working days.

@block signature
{officer.full_name}
{officer.title}
{officer.work_email}
